{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And it was the day</b> — The Gaon [Saadia] said: The satan was a human being who was jealous of Job. And he interpreted <i>on the earth</i> as 'in his land alone.' And he interpreted <i>all that he has is in your hand</i> as 'by your choice,' and its parallel: <i>Is the hand of Joab with you?</i> And he interpreted <i>only his life preserve</i> as 'preserve yourself, so that you do not seek his life.' And he said: The angels have no jealousy. But behold, he forgot <i>and the angel of YHWH stood in the way</i> — as a satan to him. And in the book of Daniel it is explicit: <i>and none stands firm with me against these, but Michael your prince</i>. And further: <i>And I, in the first year of Darius the Mede, stood to confirm and strengthen him</i> — that is, he strengthened and helped Michael. As for clarifying the secret of these matters — a book could not contain them, and one who understands the secret of the arrays of the hosts and the variation of deeds according to the variation of the motions will know the essence of the satan, and the general principle is that he is an angel." "<b>And the meaning of: And it was the day</b> — the day of Rosh HaShanah, for all the people of the world pass before the Shekhinah like benei maron. Or it is the day of Job's judgment alone — and I cannot explain. Or its meaning is: And it was the day — on which such and such happened, as in: <i>And it was the day, and Elisha passed</i>."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "In 'as a satan to him,' the antecedent 'him' is the angel of YHWH in Balaam's donkey episode (Numbers 22); the implication is that this angel too acted as an adversary, undermining Saadia's claim that angels lack jealousy."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:33.181398720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}